[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186134291 :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le z\\le 2{x}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 2xz\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133925 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-78d73ab6-dc58-5b09-8f0f-74be4ef20e0b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134127 :question/worked-solution "![](images/c1/c1853c772e219f53a0b394bd0b50beea6b33c451afc453983cdccb1df333c5ea.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-x-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/06/0620f8f25174cb71528049341669458c68a7ccfdd3ff76b5f62c878307080419.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-x-z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}12xz\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-z}12xz\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-z}12xz\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-z}12xz\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}12xz[y]_{y=0}^{y=4-x-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}12xz(4-x-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(48xz-12{x}^{2}z-12x{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(48xz-12{x}^{2}z-12x{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(48xz-12{x}^{2}z-12x{z}^{2})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[24x{z}^{2}-6{x}^{2}{z}^{2}-4x{z}^{3}]_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(64x-24{x}^{2})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(64x-24{x}^{2})\\,dx & ={[32{x}^{2}-8{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(32-8)-0 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281291 :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}6y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1-x,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281319 :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4x\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the $z$-axis, and the curve $z+{x}^{2}=1$ in the first quadrant." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-78d73ab6-dc58-5b09-8f0f-74be4ef20e0b" :question/id #uuid "78d73ab6-dc58-5b09-8f0f-74be4ef20e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-164349" :question/problem "![](images/78/78c5b7d059cac1d2ad94edf93a3d9317a62e5c1d1c88a4be29c49bbe9dac5f39.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type III region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V=$" :question/worked-solution "For a type III region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type III region enclosed between the back surface $y={u}_{1}(x,z)=2$ and the front surface $y={u}_{2}(x,z)=6.$\n\n![](images/a0/a03d6986874a543bc21d274433b5268444f2487aea198834d379f004a7d85e79.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,2\\le y\\le 6\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $xz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\nz=1-x.\n$$\n\n![](images/06/06e8986d493efbe696751db410f84490ba634c9f68feaa03aa0bf9d71593feb3.png)\n\nHence, $D=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-x\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{2}^{6}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}[{\\int }_{2}^{6}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{x}^{2}[y]_{y=2}^{y=6}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b4d91747-a788-57b5-b27b-550a878336f2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b4d91747-a788-57b5-b27b-550a878336f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4d91747-a788-57b5-b27b-550a878336f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e774e34d-ed51-5d51-b55f-fe1ccb615316" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e774e34d-ed51-5d51-b55f-fe1ccb615316" "answer-3a1dfd9a-580f-544f-8d77-20ab90892309" "answer-8f4d7c9b-5084-5084-8274-90591e28fab4" "answer-423f4b08-f254-5350-bbe9-5a945e23b082" "answer-b3177ad2-c14f-5b29-b1fb-67e4d067ea11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e774e34d-ed51-5d51-b55f-fe1ccb615316" :answer/id #uuid "e774e34d-ed51-5d51-b55f-fe1ccb615316" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a1dfd9a-580f-544f-8d77-20ab90892309" :answer/id #uuid "3a1dfd9a-580f-544f-8d77-20ab90892309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f4d7c9b-5084-5084-8274-90591e28fab4" :answer/id #uuid "8f4d7c9b-5084-5084-8274-90591e28fab4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-423f4b08-f254-5350-bbe9-5a945e23b082" :answer/id #uuid "423f4b08-f254-5350-bbe9-5a945e23b082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3177ad2-c14f-5b29-b1fb-67e4d067ea11" :answer/id #uuid "b3177ad2-c14f-5b29-b1fb-67e4d067ea11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}8xz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b2253863-a2eb-5d06-8e91-3826f6e8edbf" :activity/id #uuid "b2253863-a2eb-5d06-8e91-3826f6e8edbf" :activity/title "Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050165 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-584a6f1d-7daa-56a7-b438-a33d62c99067" "step-d4f52355-bc41-52e2-acb1-84fccf2c578e" "step-7daf2a73-2425-568d-93d8-9ecb67de0d98" "step-c04ddbb0-06ea-5d6c-a8b3-e6a0600ff993" "step-95b50fbb-45c2-5a7d-a86b-c6b9c74dc2fa"] :activity/first-step "step-584a6f1d-7daa-56a7-b438-a33d62c99067" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-584a6f1d-7daa-56a7-b438-a33d62c99067" :step/id #uuid "584a6f1d-7daa-56a7-b438-a33d62c99067" :step/content 17592186134291 :step/next "step-d4f52355-bc41-52e2-acb1-84fccf2c578e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d4f52355-bc41-52e2-acb1-84fccf2c578e" :step/id #uuid "d4f52355-bc41-52e2-acb1-84fccf2c578e" :step/content 17592186134127 :step/next "step-7daf2a73-2425-568d-93d8-9ecb67de0d98" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7daf2a73-2425-568d-93d8-9ecb67de0d98" :step/id #uuid "7daf2a73-2425-568d-93d8-9ecb67de0d98" :step/content 17592186281291 :step/n